      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marion%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in Marion in 1857 and stayed open until 1905, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marion%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Marion Township organized in 1858, with John Case as its first chairman of supervisors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://marionmn.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The railroad chose Rochester over Marion in the 1860s, slowing the village’s growth and keeping it a quiet farming community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
